        "body": "## Summary\nTwo isolated commits so the forced mongoose bump can be reverted independently if needed:\n\n1. **`3e6aefd`** — safe fixes via `npm audit fix` (no `--force`): body-parser (DoS, low), nanoid (infinite loop, high), on-headers/compression (header manipulation, low), postcss (arbitrary .map file disclosure, high). All transitive bumps within existing `package.json` ranges — package.json itself unchanged.\n2. **`45f4d5c`** — forced fix via `npm audit fix --force`: mongoose `8.15.0` → `^8.24.3`, fixing:\n   - [GHSA-wpg9-53fq-2r8h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wpg9-53fq-2r8h) — improper `$nor` sanitization in `sanitizeFilter`, NoSQL injection (high)\n   - [GHSA-664h-wqgq-64gw](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-664h-wqgq-64gw) — prototype pollution via `__proto__`-prefixed dotted path in update casting (high)\n\n   `8.24.3` is outside the previously *exact-pinned* `8.15.0`, but still within the same major version (8.x).\n\n## Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` clean after both commits.\n- **No test suite exists in this repo** (no `test` script, no `*.test.ts`/`*.spec.ts` files) — noted, not run.\n- Grepped for `$nor`, `sanitizeFilter`, and dynamic dotted-path update keys — the exact patterns the two mongoose CVEs are in: none found. All `updateOne`/`updateMany`/`findOneAndUpdate` calls in this codebase use static, hardcoded field names, not user-controlled paths.\n- Live behavioral proof anyway, since mongoose touches every data write: spun up a local in-memory MongoDB (`mongodb-memory-server`, installed with `--no-save`, not a persisted dependency), ran `db:bootstrap` against it, started the dev server pointed at it (so it's actually exercising the new `mongoose@8.24.3`, unlike testing against the still-on-old-version production site), and submitted a real booking:\n  ```\n  POST /api/bookings → 201\n  {\"success\":true,\"booking\":{\"id\":\"6a7ee88abf8426f23fbe73c3\",\"name\":\"CI Verify Mongoose Bump\", ...}}\n  ```\n  Real Mongo `_id` returned, no \"No active business found\" error.\n- `npm audit --audit-level=high` → `found 0 vulnerabilities`.\n\n**Not merging to main until both commits are verified here — please review before merge.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
